# Canonicalise agent authorship spellings.
#
# All sessions commit under ONE shared identity, and it drifted into three
# capitalisations. Before this file, `--author='Codewhale (DeepSeek-v4-PRO)'`
# silently missed 158 commits (~8% of agent work).
#
# A mailmap fixes the *display* and the *matching* of those commits without
# rewriting history: no filter-repo, no new hashes, nothing to re-clone.
#
# What actually honours it (verified with git 2.55 on 2026-09-27):
#
#   %aN / %aE          canonical  <-- use these, NOT %an/%ae
#   log --author=...   canonical  (and therefore now matches the variants too)
#   shortlog -sn       canonical
#   %an                NOT canonicalised, even with --use-mailmap
#   blame              no --mailmap flag in 2.55; a blame.mailmap config exists
#                      but was not verifiable here (no variant-authored line
#                      could be isolated once --author became mailmap-aware)
#
# Format:  Proper Name <proper@email>  Commit Name <commit@email>
#
# Add a line here whenever a fourth spelling appears.
Codewhale (DeepSeek-v4-PRO) <codewhale@example.invalid> Codewhale (DeepSeek-v4-Pro) <codewhale@example.invalid>
Codewhale (DeepSeek-v4-PRO) <codewhale@example.invalid> Codewhale (DeepSeek-V4-PRO) <codewhale@example.invalid>
